.TH SUPER-LARA 1 "October 2026" "Super Lara" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
super-lara \- native Super Lara mods for Tomb Raider I-III Remastered
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B super-lara
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Connects to the current user's Proton game and applies selected data-only mods.
All mods start disabled. Only the explicitly supported Steam build is accepted.
Start the game normally through Steam; no sudo or Steam launch options are needed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --inspect
Read live player state without enabling mods.
.TP
.B --installations
List detected Steam libraries and Proton environments.
.TP
.B --seconds N
Duration of a command-line inspection or oxygen test.
.TP
.B --oxygen
Enable infinite oxygen in a command-line test. SIGUSR1 toggles it during the test.
.TP
.B --version
Print the application version.
.SH FILES
Settings: $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/super-lara/settings.json (default ~/.config).
.br
Logs: $XDG_STATE_HOME/super-lara/super-lara.log (default ~/.local/state).
.SH NOTES
Do not run as root. Unchecking a mod stops its writes; closing the application
stops all writes. A game update may require an updated supported-build manifest.
.SH AUTHOR
Based on Burn's Mods by burn_sours. See the packaged copyright notice.
